"ab.name": "Insooni (born Kim In-soon)",
"ab.bio2": "From the explosive energy of 'Night After Night' to the comfort carried by 'A Goose's Dream', her voice has been loved across genres and generations. She sang at New York's Carnegie Hall in 1999 and returned for a second solo concert there in 2010. In 2013 she founded Haemil School, an alternative school for teenagers from multicultural families, taking up the work of an educator alongside her music. In 2023 she took on a new challenge with KBS2's 'Golden Girls' beside fellow divas.",
"ab.hm1": "In 2013, Insooni founded <strong>Haemil School</strong> in Hongcheon, Gangwon — an alternative school for teenagers from multicultural families. True to its name, 'a clear sky after rain', it is a place that helps each child open up their own dream.",
